{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>their governor</b> — the mem is appended, and פחה and פחם are like אמנה and אמנם. Or the mem is a plural marker, and the meaning is their פחה, and this is correct, except the proper form is פחתם." "<b>the governor's bread</b> — [it is] proper to the פחה."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra addresses the unusual form פחם in Nehemiah 5:14; he tentatively proposes that the final mem may be an appended letter (as in אמנה/אמנם), but concludes it is more likely a plural suffix, though the expected plural form would be פחתם."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:08.219450068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}